   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "geometry_surface_pbl_step900",
     "description": "Surface layer, slab and YSU driven by the column geometry, stable night, step 900. WRFColumnGeometry supplies YSU's p, p8w, exner and heights above ground through its coupling-target parameters, and the lowest-layer p1, t1 and dz1 of the surface layer (p1 and t1 also the slab's p_air and t_air) by indexing the geometry column, in place of the dumped profiles and prescribed values of couplings/scm_physics_column_night.esm; the surface-layer -> slab -> YSU wiring is that document's, unchanged. Radiation is not mounted: rthraten, gsw and glw are prescribed from the same WRF suite dump. psfc stays prescribed because WRF's psfc is not the geometry's interpolated p8w(1) (they differ by about 1 Pa). References and tolerances are those of the physics-suite document (WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy, real32, merged dump esm_dump_scm_suite_900.json); the geometry state is dyn_column of fork 83347b2.",
